<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martin of Tours</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 316–397</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Saint Martin, Saint Martin of Tours</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a> was a Roman soldier turned monk and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Tours from 371 until his death in 397. Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>, he is remembered for sharing his cloak with a beggar at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amiens">Amiens</a>, and he founded the monasteries of Ligugé and Marmoutier. His shrine at Tours became one of the greatest pilgrimage centres of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, and he was adopted as the patron saint of the Frankish kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martin-of-tours.jpg" alt="Martin of Tours" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Simone Martini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simone_Martini_040.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the 4th century it became the see of <b>Saint Martin of Tours</b>, and his shrine made it one of the great pilgrimage centres of Gaul.</blockquote><a href="/state/turones">Turones</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Savaria, in what is now <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a>. Died in Candes-Saint-Martin, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=47.23,16.62&amp;year=368" aria-label="Savaria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4939 506 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Martin of Tours"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5389 776h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5389 776h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=47.23,16.62&amp;year=368">What was here in 368 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
